WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.175 --> 00:00:08.758
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:10.560
- Hey I'm Kane.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.890
I have an awesome mom

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:16.890
and you might have seen her
in a few videos in the past.

00:00:18.323 --> 00:00:20.660
- You like it?

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.923
- I love here and apparently
so do some of you.

00:00:29.164 --> 00:00:31.747
(loud popping)

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:32.960
My parents are getting older

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.085
and even though I have a
good relationship with my mom

00:00:35.085 --> 00:00:37.890
she's always see me as her youngest child

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.537
because of that I've never had

00:00:39.537 --> 00:00:41.880
a super deep conversation with her.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.953
So while my parents are still
here and happy and healthy

00:00:44.953 --> 00:00:48.360
I want to make sure I get to
know them as much as I can.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.520
So I looked up a bunch
of articles and questions

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.000
from different web sites and
I compiled a few key questions

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.583
that I have personally never ask my mom.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.623
- Okay mom.

00:01:00.628 --> 00:01:01.461
- Yes.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.294
- Welcome, hello.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:05.870
- I didn't tell my mom

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.675
what questions I was going to ask her.

00:01:07.675 --> 00:01:08.943
It's going to be a
surprise for the both of us

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:11.040
what answers I'm going to get back.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:11.943
First question.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.290
- You might have seen how my
mom and dad react to each other

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.820
and this is how they
have been my whole life.

00:01:59.295 --> 00:02:01.560
- They've been together for 40 years.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.247
Growing up, probably
seeing my parents argue

00:02:04.247 --> 00:02:07.280
maybe three times a year.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.260
That really informed a lot of
how I view relationships now.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.380
There are so many people that have said

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.700
the way Kane's dad looks at Kane's mom.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.000
They definitely make
each other better people.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.430
- So being born in America
I've always had trouble

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.710
fully understanding the
scope of what it means

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:50.160
to grow up in a war-torn country.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.364
Only a few months ago did
I sit down with my dad

00:02:53.364 --> 00:02:57.430
and ask him a few questions
about how he grew up.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.960
He casually just mentioned the fact that

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.800
he had a sibling die while at home

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.670
because the building was attacked.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.370
For me at least I grew
up pretty privileged.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.430
All I have to care about was school,

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.550
figuring out my passion and dreams.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.650
My parents were trying to figure out

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.683
how to protect their family
and trying to survive.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.530
- My mom was only able to get

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.630
elementary, middle school
education back in Vietnam.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.960
A few years ago my mom
finally had a chance

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.050
to take classes and go to school.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.080
I had never see my mom with
like a light in your eye

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.090
as much as when she got to
go to Community College.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.093
She felt really proud and
I felt really proud of her.

00:03:52.892 --> 00:03:53.920
- I am so thankful that
they made the sacrifice

00:03:55.344 --> 00:03:58.140
to come to a country
where they didn't know

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.260
the language, didn't have a community

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.470
that they could lean on

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.270
and they made a work for their kids.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.440
- I can't even imagine raising one kid

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.800
but raising nine children
in Vietnam during the war.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.632
It makes sense what my mom was saying

00:04:42.632 --> 00:04:46.823
that she just was focused
on keeping her kids alive.

00:04:47.244 --> 00:04:52.244
Mom (speaking foreign language)

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.920
- Hearing this was probably
one of the saddest things

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.060
because I know that my mom would have been

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.653
a kick-ass real estate agent.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.040
I have the privilege of
always trying to live

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.520
my life without regrets.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.430
That's only possible because

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.060
what my parents have given up.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:26.980
Does make me sad

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:29.150
because she did spend that time

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:31.300
taking care of us at home instead.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:34.807
I have memories of them collecting
soda cans from trash cans

00:05:34.807 --> 00:05:36.130
when I was younger.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:38.550
My dad working two or three jobs.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.410
Everything from like
restaurant to gardening,

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.703
delivering pizza, mechanic.

00:05:43.816 --> 00:05:44.649
(speaking a foreign language)

00:05:44.649 --> 00:05:46.193
my sister is a real estate agent.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.744
What age were you the most happy?

00:05:48.744 --> 00:05:50.693
Like everything is awesome.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.690
- I was almost a 100% sure that my mom

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.520
was going to say Chinese New Year.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:31.400
In this interview I've
learned how much my mom

00:06:31.407 --> 00:06:33.060
values just happiness.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.890
Even the expression of happiness.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:38.410
We do have epic Christmas and
Thanksgiving family parties

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:40.330
where we all go to my grandma's place.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.470
Everyone brings a giant dish

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:44.414
anywhere from like egg rolls and noodles

00:06:44.414 --> 00:06:46.300
to like KFC chicken.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.620
We just eat and chat

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.116
and my aunts would be cutting coupons

00:06:49.116 --> 00:06:52.143
for the next days discount.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.760
- I've never actually seen
her get a lottery ticket

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.210
but who doesn't want the option to retire.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:21.620
I think what I didn't realize was how much

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.107
they wanted to and are waiting to retire.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.370
- I didn't realize how much my mom

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:31.840
hesitated to plan future
enjoyment experiences.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.700
I think she's just not used
to planning that for herself.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.164
One small moment that I
remember when I was younger

00:08:37.164 --> 00:08:40.880
my mom made me this dish with
rice and meat and veggies.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:43.150
I ate it and I was full and it was good.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:45.700
I thought my mom would
just make more for herself

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.491
but instead she took my leftover rice

00:08:47.491 --> 00:08:50.430
and poured tea into it and ate that.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:52.830
As an adult looking back I realize

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.356
that my dad was working

00:08:54.356 --> 00:08:56.840
as a pizza delivery man at the time

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.280
our family was probably
struggling financially

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:02.783
and my parents just always
shielded me from it.

00:09:28.168 --> 00:09:30.248
- When I was younger
she used to have plants

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.739
and point them out and be
like hey look at my plants.

00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:36.160
And I'd be like oh cool.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.840
Now as an adult I realize how hard it is

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.210
to take care of a living plant.

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:42.250
Now going home see my mom

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.780
make these cool animal configurations

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:47.223
I'm like how do you even do that mom.

00:11:15.049 --> 00:11:17.986
- It has literally never occurred to me

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:21.990
that my mom who is mostly Chinese.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:26.683
I'm 93% Chinese, my mom
has never been to China.

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.600
- If that's something that she wants

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.970
I need to take her.

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:33.320
She definitely deserves it.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.140
- I feel like I have a
lot to show my parents now

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.390
that's outside of what
they used of just work

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.530
and I'm looking forward to doing that

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.970
with my mom and my dad.

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.364
I owe everything to her
and she deserves it.

00:11:56.364 --> 00:11:57.773
- He say, "Bye, bye.

00:11:58.287 --> 00:11:59.263
"What you say mom?

00:11:59.847 --> 00:12:01.150
"Look mom."

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:01.983
Like that.

00:12:02.292 --> 00:12:04.875
(upbeat music)

00:12:10.626 --> 00:12:13.750
- Do you think they want
to take the time to listen?

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.623
- I have no idea, we'll see.

00:12:17.005 --> 00:12:19.588
(upbeat music)

